WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:07.090
Toronto — Canada's largest city, population two point nine million, budget sixteen point three billion dollars.

00:00:07.090 --> 00:00:15.988
Five hundred million per year spent housing homeless residents in hotels with no competitive tender — per-diem rates up to one hundred and eighty dollars per night.

00:00:15.988 --> 00:00:25.954
The Eglinton Crosstown LRT has ballooned from eight point four billion to twelve point five billion, an eleven-year delay and the largest transit cost overrun in Canadian history.

00:00:25.954 --> 00:00:31.420
Meanwhile, Toronto Community Housing carries a four point eight billion dollar repair backlog.

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:32.863
This is not governance.

00:00:32.863 --> 00:00:35.397
This is institutional failure at scale.
